@* Materials and their maps.
A \emph{material} in this program is a set of up to five images of the same size, all
indexed by the same texture coordinates:

\begin{description}
\item[Color (albedo)] the base colour of the surface, stored in sRGB;
\item[Bump] a height field used only to tilt the shading normal;
\item[Displacement] a height field used to move the vertices;
\item[Specular roughness] a scalar in $[0,1]$ that controls the size of highlights;
\item[Normal map] the normal already computed by the authors of the material; we never
shade with it, but the inspector decodes it for comparison.
\end{description}

The materials are described by a \emph{manifest}, a small JSON file written by the
download script (\S\ref{fetch}). For each material it gives a name, its origin (site,
page, author and licence) and the relative paths of the available maps.

